  "slug": "ai-agents-biological-4390",
  "summary": "Static structure predictions and sequence designs are now tested against dynamics, substrate scope, and proteome-wide recoding.",
  "synthesis": "The dominant thread is testing computational protein sequence and structure outputs against more demanding criteria than a single static prediction. BILBY-PRO, evaluating 220 PROSITE-derived motifs, and BILBY-MD, an all-atom MD evaluation, show that static refolding success overstates dynamical fidelity in motif scaffolding. A proteome-scale study combines ProteinMPNN with MSA conservation to rank glutamine as the most replaceable residue, then recodes 4,148 E. coli proteins. A splicease study pairs AlphaFold3 with Rosetta to rank millions of HypX and PlpX variants for substrate scope. Peptorama, a tool for drawing and comparing non-ribosomal peptides at the peptide level, is a more tooling-oriented item in this set. What is new is the move toward dynamics-aware and large-scale assessment of design and sequence predictions.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-haiku-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-11-08"
}
